<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis bids falter slightly.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis bids falter slightly.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat eased at several locations in the U.S. High Plains, supported by a slight increase in farmer movement, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Kansas merchandisers attributed the basis move to elevators buying some wheat back from the government in this week's CCC catalog sale.</p>
<p>&quot;We had a pretty active morning yesterday because we bought some of that catalog wheat,&quot; a Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, Kansas producers continued to focus on completing harvest of the state's massive sorghum crop.  </p>
